{{also|Haben}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|habēn}} (Akin to Old Saxon {{term|hebbian|lang=osx}}, Old Norse {{term|hafa|lang=non}} (Swedish {{term|hava|lang=sv}}/{{term|ha|lang=sv}}), Old Frisian {{term|habba|lang=ofs}}, Gothic {{term|𐌷𐌰𐌱𐌰𐌽|tr=haban|lang=got|sc=Goth}}, Old English {{term|habban|lang=ang}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*habjaną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*keh₂p-||to grasp}}. Cognate with Dutch {{term|hebben|lang=nl}}, English {{term|have|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|have|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhaːbən/|[ˈhaːbən]|[ˈhaːbm̩]|lang=de}} {{a|proper standard}}
* {{IPA|/ham/|lang=de}} {{a|commonly; particularly in the present tense, occasionally also in the infinitive}}
* {{audio|De-haben.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-irregular|hat|hatte|gehabt}}

# {{context|transitive|lang=de}} To [[have]]; to [[possess]]; to [[own]].
# {{context|transitive|lang=de}} To [[have]]; to [[hold]]; to [[contain]].
# {{context|auxiliary|with a past participle|lang=de}} To [[have]]; {{non-gloss definition|forms the [[perfect tense|perfect]] and [[past perfect|past perfect tense]]}}

